<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Central Asia and the Steppe</p><h1 class="st-title">Kart dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">1245 CE – 1381 CE · capital Herat</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Tajik dynasty of maliks who rebuilt Herat after the Mongol destruction and ruled it for more than a century.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shams-al-din-muhammad-kart">Shams al-Din Muhammad Kart</a>, of a family linked to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ghurid-sultanate">Ghurid Sultanate</a>, was appointed ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herat">Herat</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> around 1245. The Mongol khan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongke">Möngke</a> confirmed him, and he and his successors became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Karts rebuilt <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herat">Herat</a>, which had been devastated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> in 1221, restoring its walls, mosques and irrigation. They ruled over Herat, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghor">Ghor</a> and parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khorasan">Khurasan</a> as maliks, balancing Ilkhanid and Chagatai pressures. After the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a> collapsed in 1335, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muizz-al-din-husayn-kart">Mu'izz al-Din Husayn Kart</a> ruled as an independent sovereign, patronising Persian scholarship and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni</a> learning.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1381 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herat">Herat</a> and deposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghiyath-al-din-pir-ali">Ghiyath al-Din Pir Ali</a>. After a revolt in 1383 the dynasty was exterminated. Herat later became the brilliant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timurid-empire">Timurid</a> capital.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kart-dynasty.jpg" alt="Kart dynasty" width="320" height="555"><figcaption>Image: Aourendil1 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Kart_dynasty_at_its_greatest_extent.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1245 CE – 1381 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Herat</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Shams al-Din Muhammad Kart, Mu'izz al-Din Husayn Kart, Ghiyath al-Din Pir Ali</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Persian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, <a href="/countries/iran">Iran</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kartids, Kurt dynasty, Maliks of Herat</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1313&amp;focus=kart-dynasty" aria-label="Kart dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6262 934 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kart dynasty lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6582 1190L7559 780M6582 1190L6134 1224M6582 1190L6582 1190"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7559 780h0M6134 1224h0M6582 1190h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6582 1190h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6582 1190h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Herat. <a href="/atlas?year=1313&amp;focus=kart-dynasty">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

